>> title: Kabis
>> category: Toppings & Pickles
>> tags: turnip, beets, pickle, middle eastern, brine
>> counters: Shawarma Counter, The Bowl Shop
>> aka: kabis, kabees, kabeis, torshi, turshi, pickled turnips, pink pickles, lift makbous, Middle Eastern pickles, the pink ones
>> pairs-with: falafel, pita-bread, hummus
>> servings: 16
>> time: 5 days
>> slack: narrow — the brine is no warmer than a hand when it is poured, because hot brine cooks the turnip soft for good
>> step.1: cut the turnips into batons
>> step.2: boil the brine, then cool it
>> step.3: pack the jar, beet at the bottom
>> step.4: ferment 4 days on the counter
>> step.5: chill 24 hr

Cut @turnips{2%lb}(900 g; peeled) into half-inch batons and @Persian cucumbers{2} into spears.

Boil @water{4%cups}(950 mL), @distilled white vinegar{1%cup}(240 mL), @pickling salt{3%Tbs}(50 g) and @granulated sugar{1%Tbs}(12 g) together for a minute in a #saucepan{}, then ~cool{30%min} until the brine is no warmer than your hand.

Pack @&(~2)cut vegetables{} into a #2-quart jar{} on top of @raw beet{1%small}(80 g; in three wedges), @garlic{4%cloves} and @bay leaves{2}, then pour @&(~1)cooled brine{} over to cover.

Ferment @&(~1)packed jar{} loosely lidded at room temperature ~stand{4%days}, out of the sun.

Chill @&(~1)pickles{} ~chill{24%hr} before the first one is eaten.
